  - ELT
abstract: >
  The Unified Habitability Index (UHI) is a probabilistic
  habitability-and-observability index: a Dirichlet-weighted geometric
  mean of seven sub-indices, evaluated by Monte Carlo over the NASA
  Exoplanet Archive pscomppars table. This release is v5.2-final
  (2026-11-18).
